# Research and working material, never published
.research/
.private/
.dev/

# Build artifacts
build/
dist/
*.o
*.d
*.a
*.so
*.egg-info/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]

# Environments
.venv/
venv/

# Editors
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp

# Models are large binaries; keep them out of git
*.beam
*.model
# Except the format fixtures, which are not artifacts but EVIDENCE. Each was
# written by the last build that emitted its format and cannot be regenerated
# -- reproducing one means checking out that commit and building it. They were
# being carried by this working tree alone, untracked, with no skip guard, so
# a fresh clone failed the compatibility tests and a `git clean -X` would have
# destroyed the only copies. 1.9 MB total.
!tests/fixtures/*.beam

# Verification evidence IS tracked; only the rebuildable fixture is not.
!verification/

# The runtime profile: the tool is tracked, its output is not. A measurement
# belongs to the machine that took it -- runs/ is tens of MB of timings,
# cache/ holds built models, and TIMINGS.md is regenerated from runs/ on every
# invocation, so tracking it would churn a table nobody reads in a diff.
tools/runtime_profile/runs/
tools/runtime_profile/cache/
tools/runtime_profile/TIMINGS.md
tools/runtime_profile/*.log

# Benchmarks design and working notes
benchmarks/*.md
benchmarks/runs/


